  "id": "emotional-processing-theory",
  "term": "emotional processing theory",
  "definition": "Emotional processing theory is a view of exposure-based therapy that says improvement happens as conditioned fear links weaken and a person’s fear or distress decreases during an exposure session and across repeated sessions. In this account, habituation within and between sessions is a key process behind treatment effects.",
